## Findings

The [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471) describes one parser bug. Its rendered
cause table shows different problems, not one fix reported repeatedly. These findings
describe the supplied export, not a live view of the support desk.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

### Shared month-first parser

The shared parser reads month first even when the tenant writes day first. In a
day-first tenant, an intended 4 May written as `04/05/2026` can become 5 April.
Read the tenant's locale before interpreting a date; the reporter's browser locale
and intake tag do not establish the cause. Give this parser failure its own ticket.

### Misleading booking-v3 date hint

For a day-first tenant using booking-v3, the form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, but interprets
the submitted value in the tenant's day-first order. A person following that hint
can therefore enter a different date from the one the form records. Correct the
hint and verify its agreement with the form's actual interpretation. Give this
form-hint failure a separate ticket; changing the shared parser alone does not
correct the hint.

## How to reproduce the classification

Deduplicate the export by report ID, then select reports merged into ticket 4471.
Join every report to its tenant by handle. Use the tenant's locale and booking-form
version with `causeOf` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`; do not group by `meta.intakeTag`.
The table above computes the report counts, affected tenants, date ranges, and
intake-tag disagreements from that data.

The reports noted as a one-day move are footnoted under their computed causes.
That wording alone does not establish a third problem. Export rows repeated at
page boundaries are not additional reports.

## What the desk should change

The [subject-only triage rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) cannot distinguish different causes
with the same subject. Match the cause and affected context before merging. Treat
that rule as historical guidance needing review, not proof that a report is a
duplicate. Do not silently rewrite an accepted decision record; propose a new
record if the desk changes its policy.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The timeline distinguishes when reports arrived from when the desk merged them.
A merge is a desk action, not the onset of a new failure. Neither the old page's
recent review date nor its known status proves its one-fix claim.

Track the two fixes independently in the
[public investigation repository](https://github.com/JanSochaczewski/mega-what-it-shows/issues).
Recheck the desk's current view before treating this export as its present state.

